    "preserved_mechanism": "A chunk summary belongs to its last packed sequence. The state-passing loop uses chunk endpoint seq_idx to gate the decayed incoming state; token outputs combine local results with gated incoming chunk states."
  },
  "adaptations": [
    "Standalone forward diagonal recurrence using precomputed per-token injection vectors u and positive decay, not the full Mamba projection/convolution/outer-product layer.",
    "Retain chunk-local summary, sequential cross-chunk state passing and per-token carry-combination stages, with FP32 storage and channel masking.",
    "Replace logarithmic decay cumsums plus exp with direct products of supplied decays to isolate sequence identity composition from exp approximation.",
    "Use direct chunk-local recurrence instead of upstream tensor-dot local contractions; the chunk endpoint ownership and downstream carry consumption are retained.",
    "Bound B,L,H,D and stable decay for a small T4 pilot; remove autotuning, backward paths and optional non-packed dispatch. Add executable public input validation and independent FP64 serial reference.",
    "Both versions have identical complete contracts, public references, convenience generators, validation and licenses. The sole between-version code change selects a chunk start instead of endpoint for state-passing identity."
  ],
  "synthetic_mutation": {
    "location": "_pass_states representative index",
    "case_112": "min((chunk+1)*K,L)-1",
    "case_113": "chunk*K",
    "effect": "When a chunk contains a sequence boundary, its last-sequence state summary can be combined with an earlier sequence carry; later per-token combination exposes cross-sequence contamination. Reset branches and output sequence gating remain present."
  },
  "domain_rationale": "Input representation exclusions are declared identically before evaluation; no grad/inference/lazy flags or subclasses. validate_inputs is actually called by run. Labels are nondecreasing with unique segment identity, consistent with packed sequences.",
  "numerical_argument": {
    "exact_bound": "For |initial|<=1, |u|<=1 and 0.5<=decay<=31/32, the absolute state and the sum of absolute weighted contributions are <=32 (33 is a conservative bound).",
    "rounding_bound": "For L<=257, K<=64 and at most17 chunks, the multiply/add dependency paths in the three-stage polynomial have fewer than720 FP32 roundings. gamma720*33 is about0.001417, below the absolute tolerance0.002. The extra1e-4*|target| adds margin. Underflow contributions are negligible at this scale; intermediate values stay finite. No tensor-core operations or approximate exponentials are used and FP fusion is disabled.",
    "algebra": "Monotone sequence labels make endpoint equality equivalent to uninterrupted same-sequence carry across a chunk. Local summaries reset internally; token carry is applied only to the leading sequence. Independent per-segment weighted sums and serial recurrence establish no cross-sequence term in the target.",
    "limitation": "This is a reviewed error-bound argument and finite qualification, not a machine-checked proof."
  },
